🔄 Step 6️⃣ — Sequence Flow (Interaction)
1️⃣ Vehicle Entry Flow
Vehicle → EntranceGateController
          ↓
   ParkingService.findAvailableSpot(vehicleType)
          ↓
   Assign spot + mark occupied
          ↓
   Ticket generated and returned

2️⃣ Vehicle Exit Flow
Vehicle → ExitGateController
          ↓
   Ticket validated
          ↓
   RateCalculator.calculate(ticket)
          ↓
   PaymentService.processPayment()
          ↓
   Mark spot available again


🎯 Tip: Always describe the sequence clearly — interviewers love this.

🔧 Step 7️⃣ — Add Cross-Cutting Concerns
Concern	How We Handle It
Concurrency	Use locks on spot allocation (synchronized block or DB transactions)
Extensibility	Add new VehicleType easily (enum-based or strategy)
Scalability	Each floor handled by microservice / partitioned by floorId
Caching	Cache available spots count in Redis
Payment Integration	PaymentService can integrate with 3rd-party payment gateway
Error Handling	Throw custom exceptions (e.g., NoAvailableSpotException)
Persistence	Use DB with spot, ticket, payment tables
Logging & Monitoring	Log each entry/exit, expose metrics per floor
